WEBVTT

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:06.381
Cool, so we've set it
up so that when our

00:00:06.393 --> 00:00:14.720
player runs into an obstacle,
it'll start the death animation.

00:00:14.721 --> 00:00:17.462
But there is one small
problem that we actually

00:00:17.474 --> 00:00:19.760
need to fix, which
is when we press the

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:24.771
spacebar, we're actually
still able to jump and that's

00:00:24.772 --> 00:00:32.680
definitely not something
that should be possible.

00:00:32.681 --> 00:00:35.330
So we're going to need
to change our code just

00:00:35.342 --> 00:00:38.120
a little bit so that way
we don't just magically

00:00:38.121 --> 00:00:42.920
jump even though technically the
game is over and the player has died.

00:00:42.921 --> 00:00:45.450
Now in order to prevent
our player from jumping

00:00:45.462 --> 00:00:47.680
over and over again
when the game is over

00:00:47.681 --> 00:00:52.600
and they've lost, we'll actually need to
change the condition of our if statement.

00:00:53.349 --> 00:00:56.000
So perfectly fine that
they press spacebar and

00:00:56.012 --> 00:01:00.040
they can jump and to make sure that
they are on the ground when they jump.

00:01:00.041 --> 00:01:03.794
But we do need to make
sure that the game is not over

00:01:03.795 --> 00:01:08.400
otherwise they'll still be able
to jump when the game is over.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:12.029
So we're going to add
an and symbol here, so

00:01:12.041 --> 00:01:15.600
two ampersands for
and and then we're going

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:24.400
to use if game over equals equals false.

00:01:24.401 --> 00:01:28.520
So if the game is not
over then this thing will run.

00:01:28.569 --> 00:01:33.040
In fact there's actually an
easier way that we can do this.

00:01:33.041 --> 00:01:41.000
So we can actually use what's called
an exclamation point and set this to true.

00:01:41.001 --> 00:01:47.840
So in this case the exclamation point
actually negates the statement after it.

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:52.840
So if game over is not equal to true.

00:01:52.841 --> 00:01:59.760
So the same thing as saying game over equals
equals false, then it will do this thing.

00:01:59.761 --> 00:02:06.000
In fact there's actually even a shorter way
that we can write if the game is not over

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:10.137
for Boolean values
we can actually just put

00:02:10.149 --> 00:02:14.240
that exclamation point
in front of game over.

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:18.473
So in this case this
says if the game is not

00:02:18.485 --> 00:02:22.440
over because of this
exclamation point then

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.160
do these lines of code.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:34.360
Now if I save we can see if this code
really worked when we press play.

00:02:34.361 --> 00:02:36.820
So if we press space
we can still jump and

00:02:36.832 --> 00:02:39.480
then if we hit one of
the barriers the player

00:02:39.481 --> 00:02:44.920
runs into it and then we press the
space bar and we can't jump anymore.

00:02:44.921 --> 00:02:48.145
So a really easy way
that we can prevent the

00:02:48.157 --> 00:02:51.320
player from jumping
after the game is over.

00:02:51.321 --> 00:02:57.960
So what you're going to do is in your update
method in the player controller you're

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:02.649
going to add in your if
statement another and

00:03:02.661 --> 00:03:06.680
comparison so you can
chain them all together.

00:03:06.681 --> 00:03:13.800
So if the space bar is down and the player
is on the ground and the game is not over

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:19.640
so all of these have to be
true then this will happen.

00:03:19.641 --> 00:03:20.641
Now it's your turn.